# Fixed 2026-10-29, defect 2258, lane c-boundary (panel 230's R1, panel 232's R6,
# *saying why and where*): `==` on a dead C handle.
# Symptom: `kept == a`, after a helper taking `a` with `@` gave it back,
# stopped at 134 with its sentence and no `at <file>:<line>:<column>, in
# <function>`: `hero_handle_eq` had no `_at` entry point.
# Cause: the one stop of a program's own operation panel 230 did not reach.
# The `==` hands its place to `hero_handle_eq_at`.

extern "fixedbugs-2258-slots.h"
    record Outer tag outer
    function make_at(i: i64) -> Outer acquires release
    function release(o: Outer consumes)

function closed(@x: Outer)
    release(o: x)

function main()
    a: Outer @= make_at(i: 0)
    kept = a
    closed(@a)
    print("kept == a: ", kept == a)
